[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      122[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Rows 1–78 are implemented in `tests/phase_b_valid_paths.rs`; the row number is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      123[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the `Case` id, so a failure message names the row directly.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      124[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      125[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Note — why some rows must use `limit = INT_MIN`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      126[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      127[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `get_bits` does `bs->pos += n` *unconditionally*, before deciding whether to
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      128[0m:[38;5;10m[49m reject. For shift residues `k >= 25` the grouped `n` exceeds 58 million, and for
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      129[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `k == 30` it is `1_879_048_195`. After two such calls `bs->pos` overflows `int`;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      130[0m:[38;5;10m[49m once it wraps negative the `> bs->limit` guard stops firing and the **C itself**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      131[0m:[38;5;10m[49m dereferences `bs->buf + (pos >> 3)` hundreds of megabytes out of bounds and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      132[0m:[38;5;10m[49m segfaults. That is a fault in the C for those inputs, not a translation
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      133[0m:[38;5;10m[49m difference.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      134[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      135[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Setting `bs->limit = INT_MIN` makes `pos > limit` true for every `pos` except
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      136[0m:[38;5;10m[49m exactly `INT_MIN`, so `get_bits` always takes its early-out and never touches
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      137[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the buffer. The full `ba` domain (all 32 shift residues, the `2 << 30` signed
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      138[0m:[38;5;10m[49m overflow, `mod == 1`, the `code % mod - mod / 2` cast) is therefore compared
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      139[0m:[38;5;10m[49m read-free in rows 60–72 and 76, while rows that *do* read the buffer have their
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      140[0m:[38;5;10m[49m reachable `k` capped by `kcap_for()` in `tests/common/mod.rs` so `bs->pos`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      141[0m:[38;5;10m[49m provably cannot overflow. `kcap_remap()` preserves the *magnitude* of `ba` while
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      142[0m:[38;5;10m[49m lowering its residue, so high `ba` values are still exercised on the read path.
